>> title: Relleno de Piña
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: pineapple, filling, mexican, piloncillo, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: relleno de pina, relleno de piña, pineapple filling, mermelada de piña, mermelada de pina, pina filling
>> pairs-with: empanadas-de-pina, bigotes-de-pina
>> servings: 16
>> time: 2 hr 50 min
>> step.1: simmer 25 min, until jammy
>> step.2: thicken with the slurry, 2 min
>> step.3: stir in the lime, cool and chill 2 hr

Simmer @fresh pineapple{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; peeled, cored and chopped small), @grated piloncillo{5%oz}(140 g), @cinnamon stick{1} and @water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) in a wide pan ~simmer{25%min}, stirring near the end, until the fruit has collapsed and the pan draws a clean line behind the spoon. The same table with squash gives relleno de calabaza and with sweet potato gives camote — one filling, three shelf names.

Stir @cornstarch{1%Tbs}(8 g) slaked in @cold water{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)pineapple jam{} and ~thicken{2%min} at a bubble. It has to hold a fold inside a pastry without running out of the crimp.

Stir @lime juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into @&(~1)thickened filling{} to sharpen it, fish out the cinnamon stick, cool it to room temperature and ~chill{2%hr}. Warm filling melts the fat out of the dough it is going into.
